From 3609623275fd34ae8e2f225b1f11707240d1389c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 20:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 480/572] fix(st): make STM32MP1X/STM32MP2X boolean flags

Instead of defining those 2 flags with TF_CFLAGS += -D<flag>, use the
call assert_booleans/add_defines helpers. The #ifdef in C files are
changed to #if.
And to avoid flags being unset, always define all the SoC flags whatever
the platform is. This avoid warnings when -Wunused flag is set.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git f0c11706ec63f02594e63552ab6ed2f90701f684 fix(st): make STM32MP1X/STM32MP2X boolean flags]
